'''Sardis Ramsin''', [[Operating number|designated]] '''TD-7556''', was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] who served in the [[Desert stormtrooper|sandtrooper]] division of the [[Stormtrooper Corps]], in the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Imperial Army|army]].<ref name="Born in the Storm" /> At some point, he was on [[Weigh Station Karambola]], where he received a beating from a group of [[Rodian]]s led by [[Bludlow]] after posing as a [[bounty hunter]].<ref name="Last Shot" />

Around [[1 BBY]],<ref name="IV Date">{{FilmDate|IV|1}}</ref> he was stationed at [[Mos Eisley]], [[Tatooine]], as part of [[Commander]] [[Wanten|TD-110's]] [[Foot Patrol 7]]. After an incident involving the escape of a [[freighter]] carrying [[droid]]s wanted by the Empire, Ramsin, who had harbored a desire to ride [[dewback]]s and hated his job and comrades, [[Desertion|deserted]] and sent a sarcastically-worded incident report as his final communication to his former superiors.<ref name="Born in the Storm" />

In [[3 ABY]],<ref name="Date">The events of [[War of the Bounty Hunters – 4-LOM & Zuckuss 1|''War of the Bounty Hunters – 4-LOM & Zuckuss'' 1]] take place during ''[[Star Wars: War of the Bounty Hunters]]'', which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of to [[3 ABY]].</ref> Ramsin acted as a broker between a [[Jawa]] [[scavenger]] and the [[warlord]] [[Cribiriz Idollax]], arranging for the former's delivery of the head of bounty hunter droid [[4-LOM]] to the latter.<ref name="4&Z">[[War of the Bounty Hunters – 4-LOM & Zuckuss 1|''War of the Bounty Hunters – 4-LOM & Zuckuss'' 1]]</ref>

